# loopctl config — TuiRedesign builder (KIND=runner). Generated by `loopctl init`.
# Committed copy so the loop travels with the repo. To run it yourself: copy this file and
# tui-redesign.prompt into your loopctl checkout's loops/ directory, then set TARGET to your
# lazyaws clone path and LOG to any writable file. Without loopctl, see "Running the loop" in
# ../spec.md for the bare-claude fallback.
NAME="TuiRedesign"
KIND=runner
# PROVIDER=codex runs cycles on `codex exec` instead of `claude -p` (single account, ledgers $0,
# no USD budgets — see README). Omitted here means claude.
TARGET="/Users/noelruault/go/src/github.com/noelruault/lazyaws"
BRANCH="tui-redesign"
SOURCE=""
DOCS="docs/tui-redesign"
LOG="/Users/noelruault/go/src/github.com/noelruault/lazyaws/.backups/tui-redesign.log"
# Effectively disabled (24h). A 30-minute kill discarded a whole cycle's reasoning and — worse —
# was indistinguishable from a cycle that simply returned nothing: it logged a blank summary and
# still consumed one of N. Until there is a real answer (surface the kill, forgive the cycle, and
# have cycles commit incrementally so only the current step is lost), a big group is better left to
# finish than cut off. Kept non-zero so a genuinely hung cycle still dies eventually.
CYCLE_TIMEOUT=86400
DEFAULT_MAX=100000

# THE CYCLE ITSELF ALWAYS RUNS STRONG. A cycle is the main thread: it decides what the work IS,
# holds the contract, and is accountable for the gate. Routing it down to a cheap model to save money
# buys a wrong decision made confidently, which costs more than it saves. So MODEL is the floor and
# the route table varies only EFFORT, never the model — an easy group thinks less, it does not think
# worse. Savings come from DELEGATION inside the cycle (see the prompt: router run), where bulk
# mechanical steps go to cheap models under a plan this thread wrote.
MODEL="opus"
# No ROUTES: the vendored router (v0.1.1) parses only <range>:<model> and splits on the LAST colon,
# so the three-field effort form the newer source documents fails here with a bad-range error. With
# MODEL pinned there is nothing left for a model-only table to vary, so the line is omitted rather
# than left as a no-op that breaks loopctl status. Restore effort routing by bumping router.
